#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:42
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:44
msgid ""
"This command shows what packages are currently installed in a profile. For "
"each installed package, it shows the following information:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:48
msgid ""
"`Name`: A unique name used to unambiguously identify the package in "
"invocations of `nix profile remove` and `nix profile upgrade`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:52
msgid ""
"`Index`: An integer that can be used to unambiguously identify the package "
"in invocations of `nix profile remove` and `nix profile upgrade`. "
"(_Deprecated, will be removed in a future version in favor of `Name`._)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:56
msgid ""
"`Flake attribute`: The flake output attribute path that provides the package "
"(e.g. `packages.x86_64-linux.hello`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:59
msgid ""
"`Original flake URL`: The original (\"unlocked\") flake reference specified "
"by the user when the package was first installed via `nix profile install`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:63
msgid ""
"`Locked flake URL`: The locked flake reference to which the original flake "
"reference was resolved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-list.md:66
msgid "`Store paths`: The store path(s) of the package."
msgstr ""

